config BLINKY_BARE_METAL_GPIO
	bool "Toggle led0/probe0 by writing GPIO registers directly"
	help
	  When enabled, the blink loop drives led0 and probe0 by writing the
	  GPIO port's OUTSET/OUTCLR registers directly instead of calling
	  gpio_pin_toggle_dt(). Pin setup still uses the Zephyr GPIO API.

config BLINKY_PROBE_P7_00
	bool "Toggle P7.00 in the blink loop"
	default y
	help
	  When enabled, the blink loop toggles P7.00 (the probe0 pin) so it can
	  be probed. When disabled, P7.00 is left low. Independent of
	  BLINKY_PROBE_P9_00.

config BLINKY_FLPR_VIO
	bool "Drive P7.00 through FLPR's VIO"
	depends on SOC_NRF54H20_CPUFLPR && BLINKY_PROBE_P7_00
	help
	  Set this through SB_CONFIG_BLINKY_FLPR_VIO in sysbuild.conf, which
	  also routes P7.00 to FLPR's VIO in UICR; sysbuild overrides any value
	  set here. The blink loop then drives P7.00 with VIO CSR writes,
	  whichever toggle method is selected. P9.00 is unaffected.

config BLINKY_PROBE_P9_00
	bool "Toggle P9.00 in the blink loop"
	help
	  When enabled, the blink loop toggles P9.00 so it can be probed. On
	  the nRF54H20 DK, P9.00 is the led0 pin, so LED0 flickers while the
	  loop runs. When disabled, P9.00 is left low. Independent of
	  BLINKY_PROBE_P7_00.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
